# Skills

## Consumer skills (shipped)

- `packages/permdock/skills/wire-permdock/SKILL.md`: how to add PermDock to an app (define, policy, factory file, first guard, MCP / AI SDK wiring, `permdock doctor`). Written for the consumer's repo; `adapters.md` next to it holds the adapter factory shapes.
- `packages/permdock/skills/audit-permissions/SKILL.md`: how to review an existing PermDock setup (ungranted permissions, unused definitions, closures that could be portable, snapshot scope, OWASP ASI02 / ASI03 checklist).
- Consumer instructions never go in `AGENTS.md` or `.agents/rules`, and maintainer instructions never go in these skills.
- Frontmatter follows the [Agent Skills spec](https://agentskills.io/specification): `name` (matches the folder), `description` (what it does and when to use it, third person), `license: MIT`, and `metadata` with `author`, `homepage` and `repository` as strings. No version in `metadata`: skills version with the `permdock` package.
- They reach users three ways, all from the same folders: `npx skills add ScaleDockHQ/PermDock`, `permdock skills` from `node_modules/permdock/skills`, and the Claude Code plugin in `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` (`/plugin marketplace add ScaleDockHQ/permdock`). Adding a skill updates the marketplace `skills` array, `cli/skills.mdx` and `for-ai-agents.mdx`.
- `npx skills add ScaleDockHQ/PermDock --list` must list only `wire-permdock` and `audit-permissions`. Run it after touching skill folders or the marketplace file.

## Vendored skills (maintainer tooling)

- `.agents/skills/` holds third-party skills for agents working in this repo, pinned by source and hash in `skills-lock.json`. `.cursor/skills` and `.claude/skills` symlink into it.
- Refresh or add one with `npx skills add <source> --skill <name>`, which updates the lock. Never edit a vendored skill in place; the next update overwrites it.
- They are hidden from ripgrep (`.ignore`) and from Cursor indexing (`.cursorignore`) because each match would appear three times; skills load by path.
- If `skills add … --list` ever shows a vendored skill to consumers, stop committing `.agents/skills`: gitignore it and restore it from `skills-lock.json` on install.
